  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Bonporteau is one of Cavalaire-sur-Mer's beaches, with fine sand and easy access from the town centre. During the day it fills up like every beach in the resort in summer — it's more in the late afternoon and evening that it becomes a real playground for dogs.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the official rule published by the Cavalaire-sur-Mer tourist office (cavalairesurmer.fr), dogs — even on a leash — are banned from all of the town's beaches from 6am to 10pm from 1 April to 31 October, and from 10am to 5pm from 1 November to 31 March. Outside those slots, they are allowed on a leash. In practice: in summer, the usable window is limited to the night (10pm-6am); in winter, it is much wider (5pm-10am, almost the whole day except the midday slot). The same rule applies across all of the town's beaches, including the <a href="/en/fiche-grande-plage-cavalaire">town-centre beach</a> a little further east.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in summer, enjoy a moonlit walk on the sand from 10pm — it's when the beach is calmest. Off-season, the window runs from 5pm to 10am the next day: plenty of time for a late-afternoon or early-morning outing. The Corniche des Maures loop (see "Nearby" below) remains walkable with your dog at any time: only the beach itself is subject to these hours, not the trail.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cavalaire-sur-Mer's town centre is a few minutes' walk away, with its café terraces and market, handy for extending the walk after the beach. Bonporteau also sits on the route of the Corniche des Maures, a coastal trail that crosses the Fenouillet valley — a protected natural site listed as national heritage, between bamboo groves and holm oaks. A marked loop of about 1.4 km starts from the beach, crosses the forest and comes back above Bonporteau: a nice option for extending the walk with your dog before or after swimming. The Chemin Pierre Foncin car park, on the road above, also gives direct access (distance to be checked on-site).</p>
    </div>

